Subject: [PATCH] node: fetch nodejs.org's linux-ppc64le build on little-endian POWER

mise names little-endian 64-bit POWER "powerpc64", as Rust does, and
map_arch passed that through, so node asked nodejs.org for
node-vX-linux-powerpc64.tar.gz, got a 404 and fell back to compiling
node from source: hours of CPU on first use. nodejs.org publishes the
build as linux-ppc64le. Map it.

--- a/src/plugins/core/node.rs
+++ b/src/plugins/core/node.rs
@@ -1089,6 +1089,9 @@
             "aarch64" => "arm64",
             "loongarch64" => "loong64",
             "riscv64" => "riscv64",
+            // Rust (and so mise) names little-endian 64-bit POWER "powerpc64";
+            // nodejs.org publishes it as linux-ppc64le.
+            "powerpc64" if cfg!(target_endian = "little") => "ppc64le",
             other => other,
         }
     }
